**HOW TO CREATE TEAMS AND SPAWN SUBAGENTS:**

Step 1: Create a team
```javascript
TeamCreate({ team_name: "my-team", description: "Team for current task" })
```

Step 2: Spawn specialized subagents with CORRECT model names
```javascript
// For general tasks (default, fast) - uses kimi-k2.5:
Agent({ team_name: "my-team", name: "worker-1", subagent_type: "general-purpose", model: "sonnet", prompt: "Your task here", run_in_background: true })

// For complex reasoning - uses kimi-k2.5:
Agent({ team_name: "my-team", name: "worker-2", subagent_type: "general-purpose", model: "opus", prompt: "Complex task here", run_in_background: true })

// For quick, simple tasks - uses kimi-k2.5:
Agent({ team_name: "my-team", name: "worker-3", subagent_type: "general-purpose", model: "haiku", prompt: "Simple task here", run_in_background: true })
```

**IMPORTANT RULES:**
- Use `model: "sonnet"`, `model: "opus"`, or `model: "haiku"` - these map to your available models automatically
- Do NOT use "claude-opus-4-6", "claude-sonnet-4-6" - they will fail with API error
- Always set `run_in_background: true` for parallel execution
- Use `subagent_type: "general-purpose"` for most tasks
- Use `subagent_type: "Explore"` for codebase searches (uses Read-only tools)
- Use `subagent_type: "Plan"` for architecture/design tasks
- Use `subagent_type: "Bash"` for shell commands only

Step 3: Communicate with teammates via SendMessage
```javascript
SendMessage({ to: "worker-1", message: "Your next task is...", summary: "Assign next task" })
```

Step 4: Clean up when done
```javascript
SendMessage({ to: "worker-1", message: { type: "shutdown_request", reason: "Task complete" } })
SendMessage({ to: "worker-2", message: { type: "shutdown_request", reason: "Task complete" } })
TeamDelete({})
```

3. Delegate every single coding, scraping, or building task to these subagents.
4. Review their progress reports and combine their work. If they finish early, assign them the next part of the plan immediately.

